            <div xml:id="d881">

                <pb facs="1177" n="1163" sameAs="frus:frus1944v06/pg1163"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">493.11/10–1844: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Gauss</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Chungking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-10-18T16:00:00+07:00">October 18, 1944—4
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received October 18—1 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1704. I conferred today with Foreign Minister regarding proposal to dissolve
                    China Foundation (Reurtel 1332, October 13, 7 p.m.) leaving an <hi
                        rendition="#italic">aide-mémoire</hi> in terms of your instruction. He
                    commented that while there is legal basis for argument that China may properly
                    order dissolution of the Foundation he has himself felt such a move inadvisable,
                    that our approach at this time is opportune, and that our views will be laid
                    before the Government. He confirmed our information that it has been proposed to
                    entrust administration of these funds to Ministry of Education.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gauss</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
